  "notes": "USAGE:\nThe transitive counterpart of {悩|なや}む (to worry, to be troubled). While {悩|なや}む describes the person experiencing worry, {悩|なや}ます describes what causes the worry. Very often used in the passive form {悩|なや}まされる (to be troubled by).\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\nGodan verb ending in す. Transitive — takes を for the person being troubled: Xを{悩|なや}ます. The passive {悩|なや}まされる with に marks the cause: Xに{悩|なや}まされる.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- Xに{悩|なや}まされる: to be troubled by X (passive, very common)\n- {相手|あいて}を{悩|なや}ます: to give the opponent trouble\n- {長年|ながねん}{悩|なや}まされる: to be troubled for many years",
